@tradition lightdisc-cup
// W3 rec deck words. Every 4 weeks from Day 28, Sunday 11:30-16:30, in Winner Stays On's place; singles bracket (lead 17's call 2: you and a friend both enter); Pell runs it, the foyer's Cup board.
== mail
- The Lightdisc Cup is tomorrow, {time} at the court, in place of Winner Stays On. Pell's bracket is up in the foyer. Play your matches, cheer the rest, and see whose name goes on the Cup board.
== ask
- Cup day! I've been practising my backhand on the bunk room door. Sorry, bunk.   #funny
- Are you in the Cup? I drew someone from the Watch. They don't blink.   #funny
- Lightdisc Cup today. Bring a friend and your loudest cheer.
== here
- Quarter-finals! The bracket's on the board.
- Come on, Works! Or whoever. Come on, someone!   #funny
- That's a match point. Nobody breathe.
== thanks
- You join the crowd in the stands for the Cup. Pell chalks up the bracket and rings the bell for the first match.
== chatter
- Who won the Cup? I still can't believe that final.
- My department went out in the first round. We're calling it a warm-up.   #funny
- The Cup board's got a new name on it. Go and look.
